ns and Remote catalogs as Chat, and\nwr"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"ites through `session.selectModel` / `/permission <preset>`; switching to\nfull access asks for the s"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"ame risk confirmation.\n- **Slash commands and `@` references.** A `/command` line runs through\n`sess"},{"id":"p6s9","text":"ion.command` without spending a turn, and `@` lists files and sessions\nthrough the public reference "},{"id":"p6s10","text":"providers before inserting the same plain-text\ntoken Chat uses.\n- **Approvals and questions answer i"},{"id":"p6s11","text":"n the tile.** An approval or\n`ask_user_question` waiting on that Session replaces the composer with "},{"id":"p6s12","text":"a\ncompact card; answering calls the same pending object Chat's panel uses.\n- **Context occupancy.** "},{"id":"p6s13","text":"The footer shows the same `projected / window` token\nreading as Chat, and hides itself when the proj"},{"id":"p6s14","text":"ection is absent.\n- **Session or project per tile.** Pin one session, or pin a project and switch\nbe"},{"id":"p6s15","text":"tween that project's sessions inside the tile; a free tile's picker puts the\nproject badge on every "},{"id":"p6s16","text":"row (the same badge as the header) and filters by title\nor project, with arrow keys and Enter.\n- **A"},{"id":"p6s17","text":"rchiving frees the tile.** Archive a session in the sidebar and any tile\nholding it lets go as soon "},{"id":"p6s18","text":"as the Host confirms the archive (one update later;\nthe grid keeps no optimistic copy): a session ti"},{"id":"p6s19","text":"le empties, a project tile only\ndrops the session and keeps its scope. Archived sessions leave the t"},{"id":"p6s20","text":"ile pickers\nand drop resolution, and come back when you unarchive them.\n- **Real-time status.** A do"},{"id":"p6s21","text":"t on each title shows whether the session is working,\nand a colored project badge before the title k"},{"id":"p6s22","text":"eeps the Session's project\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## How sessions are wired"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Sessions come from the public `ctx.sessions` API (`list`, `retain`, the event\nsource), and input goe"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"s out through `session.prompt`. Each tile's transcript,\nMarkdown, tool cards, and composer are rende"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"red by this plugin itself, with\nstyles built on DSH's theme variables and visual rules so they match"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"is plugin itself, with\nstyles built on DSH's theme variables and visual rules so they match the app."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Everything DSH-specific is consumed through public services and Remote\nnamespaces — `ctx.fileUpload`"},{"id":"p9s2","text":", `ctx.uiSession`, `ctx.remote.session`,\n`ctx.remote.permissionPresets`, `ctx.remote.fileReferences`"},{"id":"p9s3","text":", and\n`ctx.remote.sessionReferenceResolver` — with one deliberate exception: clearing\nthe completion"},{"id":"p9s4","text":" dot. DSH clears `completionUnread` only for the main view and\nexposes no write path, so the tile re"},{"id":"p9s5","text":"ads the `uiSession` instance's own\nacknowledgement set (`completionUnread` plus `publishStatus()`). "},{"id":"p9s6","text":"The reasoning and\nthe fallback are in TECH 13.5, and the plugin\nmoves to the public method as soon a"},{"id":"p9s7","text":"d\nthe fallback are in TECH 13.5, and the plugin\nmoves to the public method as soon as DSH ships one."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"`test/dsh-contract.test.js` asserts those methods and type names — the two private\nmembers included "},{"id":"p10s2","text":"— against the installed DSH build, so an upstream rename fails a\ngate with the exact missing symbol "},{"id":"p10s3","text":"instead of silently breaking a tile; when the\nprivate members are gone the dot simply stays lit. Set"},{"id":"p10s4","text":" `DSH_CONTRACT_ROOT` to\ncheck another installation; the test skips when no DSH install is present."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"## Requirements"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- DeepSeek Harness **0.2.1-rc.2** or newer (desktop or web).\n- Desktop app or `dsh web`; the same bu"},{"id":"p12s2","text":" **0.2.1-rc.2** or newer (desktop or web).\n- Desktop app or `dsh web`; the same build works in both."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Then restart the app (or reload the web page). The toggle appears at the bottom\nof the sidebar, next"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"app (or reload the web page). The toggle appears at the bottom\nof the sidebar, next to your account."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Installing from a local checkout"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"## Use"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"| Action | Where |"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"| Enter or leave split view | Left-click the ⊞ at the sidebar's bottom |\n| Choose the grid | Right-c"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"lick that same ⊞ |\n| Assign a session | Use a tile's header picker, or drag a session row from the s"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"idebar into the tile |\n| Rename a session | The ✎ next to the tile's title |\n| Resize text in one ti"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"le | `Ctrl` + wheel over that tile |\n| Raise the cell limit | Settings → General → Split grid |"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"The cap defaults to 10 cells for the whole screen (12 hard limit per window,\nboth configurable). Six"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" cells fit comfortably; past six, opening more asks for\nconfirmation."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"`packages/dsh-workspace-split/src/client.js` is the source. `client.js` next to\nit is generated and "},{"id":"p24s2","text":"not tracked by git — `npm install` in that package builds it\nthrough `prepare`, and `npm run build` "},{"id":"p24s3","text":"rebuilds it. Never edit it by hand."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"See AGENTS.md for the repository rules and docs/ for the\nproduct and design notes."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}

